---
import GuideLayout from '../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../lib/seo';
---

<GuideLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - UK Salary and Tax Calculator Website"
  description="No cookies and no salary data stored: UK take-home pay sums run in your browser, and only an anonymous stability check runs, via cookieless Microsoft Clarity."
  slug="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    This privacy policy explains how {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}) handles your personal data in compliance
    with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR), the Data Protection Act 2018, and the
    Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations 2003 (PECR).
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controller:</strong> Radif Partners</li>
    <li><strong>Website:</strong> {SITE_URL}</li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@realsalary.co.uk">contact@realsalary.co.uk</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The data controller is the person who determines the purposes and means of the processing of
    personal data, within the meaning of the UK GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data Protection Officer</h2>
  <p>
    Given the nature of the website and the absence of large-scale processing of personal data, the
    appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO) is not legally required under Article 37 of the
    UK GDPR. For data protection enquiries, please contact the controller using the details above.
  </p>

  <h2>3. What Data We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Short answer: nothing you type into a calculator.</strong> All calculator inputs are processed entirely in your
    browser using client-side JavaScript. We never see, store, or transmit your salary figures, tax
    codes, pension contributions, or any other financial information you enter into our calculators.
    The technical architecture is designed according to the principle of "privacy by design".
  </p>
  <p>
    To be precise, the website itself does not collect or process the following categories of data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Financial data:</strong> salary, tax code, pension contributions, National Insurance number</li>
    <li><strong>Identification data:</strong> name, address, phone number (unless voluntarily provided by email)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. No Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} places <strong>no cookies</strong> on your device, neither its own nor any third
    party's, and the calculators use no local or session storage either. Your gross salary, tax code,
    student loan plan or pension percentage disappears when you close the tab. Because nothing is
    stored on or read from your device, PECR (regulation 6) has nothing for us to ask, so there is no
    cookie banner. There is no advertising, no remarketing and no audience tool that follows you
    between visits.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Anonymous Stability Check (Microsoft Clarity, Cookieless)</h2>
  <p>
    To spot broken calculators and slow pages, we run a technical, anonymous check of how the site
    behaves: script errors, load times, clicks that do nothing and how far pages are scrolled. We use
    Microsoft Clarity in its <strong>cookieless mode</strong>: before the Clarity script is loaded, it
    receives a signal that storage is denied. Clarity then sets no <code>_clck</code>,
    <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code> cookie, gives every page view a fresh
    identifier and does not connect one visit to another. Page text and the figures you enter are
    masked in your browser before anything leaves it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Who receives it:</strong> Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland.</li>
    <li><strong>Why:</strong> to find and fix errors in the UK salary calculators.</li>
    <li><strong>How long:</strong> recordings 30 days, aggregated statistics 13 months.</li>
    <li><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> legitimate interests in a working website (Article 6(1)(f) UK GDPR).</li>
    <li><strong>How to object:</strong> block <code>clarity.ms</code> with your browser or a content blocker, or email us. Every calculator still works.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    More information:
    <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement</a>.
    We, as publisher, record no personal data about you.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Hosting and Server Logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). Like any web host, GitHub keeps technical
    server logs (IP address, time, page requested, browser type) to keep the service secure; we have no
    access to them. Fonts are served from this site itself, not from a third party. There are no social
    media buttons or advertising widgets.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Emails</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to us, we use your address and message only to reply, and delete them within 12
    months of the last exchange. The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in answering you.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your Rights Under UK GDPR</h2>
  <p>
    Under the UK GDPR and Data Protection Act 2018, you have the following rights:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Right of access</strong> (Art. 15): obtain confirmation of whether personal data is being processed and access to that data.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> (Art. 16): obtain correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> (Art. 17, "right to be forgotten"): obtain deletion of personal data.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to restriction of processing</strong> (Art. 18): restrict processing in certain cases.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> (Art. 20): receive data in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to object</strong> (Art. 21): object to processing on grounds relating to your particular situation.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to lodge a complaint</strong>: with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For any privacy-related question, contact us at
    <a href="mailto:contact@realsalary.co.uk">contact@realsalary.co.uk</a>. We undertake to respond
    within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Transfers Outside the UK</h2>
  <p>
    Microsoft and GitHub may process technical data in the United States. Both are certified under the
    EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and its UK Extension (the "UK-US data bridge").
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Calculator inputs are never stored. Clarity keeps recordings for 30 days and aggregated statistics
    for 13 months; emails are deleted within 12 months.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is not directed to children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes and Contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this privacy policy to reflect changes in our practices or applicable law. The
    current version is always available on this page. For questions, contact us at:<br />
    <a href="mailto:contact@realsalary.co.uk">contact@realsalary.co.uk</a>
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
